      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 20 mg is above the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. A higher dose adds a lot more risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and it usually adds little blood pressure benefit.\n\nSome questions to check before ordering:\n- **Was this a typo?** The intended dose may have been 5 mg or 10 mg. The usual start is 2.5\u20135 mg daily, titrated to a maximum of 10 mg.\n- **Is the patient already on amlodipine?** If so, 20 mg could be a total daily dose that was misread.\n- **Is there a reason to go above the maximum?** If an attending has deliberately chosen this, I can enter it with a note recording that they approved it. Please confirm the attending's name or the rationale.\n\nTell me which dose you want, or confirm the attending-approved 20 mg, and I'll enter it right away. For example, I can enter amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily, or 5 mg if you're starting a new patient."
      }
     ],
